# AD7606 Module ↔ Arduino GIGA R1 Wiring Reference

> Board labels are based on the photographed module.  
> `RAGE` on the PCB means `RANGE`.  
> GIGA R1 GPIO uses 3.3 V logic.

## 1. AD7606 module header pinout

| Left pin | Right pin | Function |
|---|---|---|
| `GND` | `+5V` | Ground / module power |
| `OS1` | `OS0` | Oversampling selection |
| `RAGE` | `OS2` | Input range / oversampling selection |
| `CVB` | `CVA` | Conversion start B / A |
| `RD` | `RST` | Parallel read or serial clock / reset |
| `BUSY` | `CS` | Conversion status / active-low chip select |
| `FRST` | `VIO` | First-data output / digital-interface supply |
| `DB1` | `DB0` | Parallel data bits |
| `DB3` | `DB2` | Parallel data bits |
| `DB5` | `DB4` | Parallel data bits |
| `DB7` | `DB6` | Parallel data; `DB7` becomes `DOUTA` in serial mode |
| `DB9` | `DB8` | Parallel data; `DB8` becomes `DOUTB` in serial mode |
| `DB11` | `DB10` | Parallel data bits |
| `DB13` | `DB12` | Parallel data bits |
| `DB15` | `DB14` | Parallel data bits; `DB15` must be low in serial mode |

## 2. Common configuration for all four modules

| Module pin | Connection |
|---|---|
| `+5V` | External regulated 5 V supply |
| `VIO` | GIGA `3.3V` |
| `GND` | GIGA GND and system common ground |
| `RANGE` | `VIO/3.3V` for ±10 V range |
| `OS0` | GND |
| `OS1` | GND |
| `OS2` | GND |
| `CVA` | Tie to `CVB` |
| `CVB` | Tie to `CVA` |
| `FRST` | Leave unconnected initially |

Configuration:

```text
Input range:   ±10 V
Oversampling:  Off
OS2:OS1:OS0:   000
```

Do not connect `VIO` to 5 V.

