# 3. Four-module 16-bit parallel mode

## Shared 16-bit data bus

Connect the same data bit from all four modules together.

| AD7606 pin on all four modules | Example GIGA pin |
|---|---:|
| `DB0` | `D22` |
| `DB1` | `D23` |
| `DB2` | `D24` |
| `DB3` | `D25` |
| `DB4` | `D26` |
| `DB5` | `D27` |
| `DB6` | `D28` |
| `DB7` | `D29` |
| `DB8` | `D30` |
| `DB9` | `D31` |
| `DB10` | `D32` |
| `DB11` | `D33` |
| `DB12` | `D34` |
| `DB13` | `D35` |
| `DB14` | `D36` |
| `DB15` | `D37` |

Example bus connection:

```text
AD7606 #1 DB0 ─┐
AD7606 #2 DB0 ─┼── GIGA D22
AD7606 #3 DB0 ─┤
AD7606 #4 DB0 ─┘
```

Repeat for `DB1` through `DB15`.

## Shared control signals

| AD7606 pin on all modules | Example GIGA pin |
|---|---:|
| `RD` | `D38` |
| Tied `CVA + CVB` | `D39` |
| `RST` | `D40` |

## Separate signals for each module

| Function | Module 1 | Module 2 | Module 3 | Module 4 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `CS` | `D41` | `D42` | `D43` | `D44` |
| `BUSY` | `D45` | `D46` | `D47` | `D48` |

Do not connect the four `BUSY` outputs together.

## Parallel acquisition sequence

```text
1. Set CS1–CS4 HIGH.
2. Pulse the shared CVA/CVB line HIGH, then LOW.
3. Wait until BUSY1–BUSY4 are all LOW.
4. Set CS1 LOW.
5. Pulse RD LOW eight times.
6. Read DB0–DB15 as one signed 16-bit value on each pulse.
7. Set CS1 HIGH.
8. Repeat for CS2, CS3 and CS4.
```

```cpp
pulseConvst();

while (
    digitalRead(BUSY1) ||
    digitalRead(BUSY2) ||
    digitalRead(BUSY3) ||
    digitalRead(BUSY4)
) {
    // Apply a timeout.
}

for (uint8_t board = 0; board < 4; board++) {
    digitalWrite(csPins[board], LOW);

    for (uint8_t channel = 0; channel < 8; channel++) {
        digitalWrite(rdPin, LOW);

        adcValues[board * 8 + channel] =
            static_cast<int16_t>(readParallelBus16());

        digitalWrite(rdPin, HIGH);
    }

    digitalWrite(csPins[board], HIGH);
}
```

